      "content": "it's definitely more about the political tension and the sheer weight of the decisions being made. i keep having this sensation of sitting in these dimly lit rooms, writing letters that could literally start or end wars. there's this specific feeling of being an advisor to someone very powerful, someone who is brilliant but perhaps a bit reckless. it's not just 'interest' in the history, it feels like i'm trying to remember a specific responsibility. could you look for diplomats or high-ranking officials from that time period who operated in that kind of shadow power or advisory role?",
